;; Glasswood's thin ice: a corridor one tile tall (no jump clears anything)
;; with three cells of thin ice in its floor (brittle: over meltwater). No
;; cell over the ice is a place to rest, so the only way over is a walk
;; that keeps going to the far bank: (engine reach)'s walk releases on
;; entering the first standable cell past the ice. Three cells from rest
;; take about 40 ticks on the ice, under BRITTLE-TICKS (60). Both ways.
(fixture
  name: "thin ice, three cells, walked over in one go"
  expect: reachable
  why: "thin ice is crossed, never rested on; three cells walk over in under a second"
  start: (5 7)
  target: ((18 7))
  brittle: ((10 8) (11 8) (12 8))
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "#########################"
   "#########################"
   "#########################"
   "#########################"
   "#########################"
   "#########################"
   "#                       #"
   "#########################"
   "##########~~~############"
   "#########################"))
